\f0\fs24 \cf0 During the my time working on the brand revival for longs drugs I came to the conclusion that in order for the brand to truly stay true to its roots in Hawaii, and pay its respects to the culture it would need a clear typeface that would prioritize olelo Hawaii as the language. \
\
Taking inspiration form modern utilitarian typefaces like Futura, Helvetica, open sans, and Proxima nova I developed the LD Sans typeface for the brand. \
\
The goal here was to create clear, legible type that could be used in serious communications like signage, announcements and products and also be used in more engaging situations like social media. After this the next goal was to make sure that certain aspects of olelo Hawaii would be the default when using this typeface so users did not have to worry about installing a language or finding another typeface that had those or worrying about how to make a home-brew version if a typeface didn\'92t have it. These aspects included the kahako on multiple letters as well as a default \'91okina rather than an apostrophe.\
\
This typeface also needed to be flexible and professional. The project was a success and longs drugs now utilizes the typeface across multiple platforms and campaigns seeing great success. }